<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/06QV">Example <span data-tag="06QV">4.7.1.7</span> <span class="named">(Truncated Objects of Homotopy Coherent Nerves)</span>.</a> Let $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ be a locally Kan simplicial category, let $X$ be an object of $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$, and let $n$ be an integer. Combining Remark <a data-tag="05ED" href="/tag/05ED">4.7.1.2</a> with Theorem <a data-tag="01LE" href="/tag/01LE">4.6.7.5</a>, we see that $X$ is $n$-truncated as an object of the homotopy coherent nerve $\operatorname{N}_{\bullet }^{\operatorname{hc}}(\operatorname{\mathcal{C}})$ if and only if, for each object $C \in \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$, the Kan complex $\operatorname{Hom}_{\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}}(C,X)_{\bullet }$ is $n$-truncated. </p>
</article>
